WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:07.400
There is one evil mastermind behind all of
the major events of Jujutsu Kaisen - and I

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:13.790
mean mastermind in the most literal way possible,
because the ultimate villain of the series

00:00:13.790 --> 00:00:15.620
is just a brain.

00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:20.460
At the end of the Shibuya Incident Arc, the
impostor pretending to be Suguru Geto revealed

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:22.900
his true identity: Kenjaku.

00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:28.000
This sorcerer has used his power to implant
his brain into other host bodies.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:30.160
And it’s not a normal brain either!

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:34.920
It’s got a freaky mouth which makes it at
least 10% more cursed.

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:41.930
Over the course of one thousand years he’s
committed all kinds of atrocities, at one

00:00:41.930 --> 00:00:45.570
point being known as the most evil sorcerer
in history.

00:00:45.570 --> 00:00:50.280
In my opinion, he’s *still* the most evil
sorcerer in history, too!

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:55.320
And not only is he the most evil sorcerer
- he’s one of the most powerful figures

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:57.680
in the world of Jujutsu Kaisen.

00:00:57.680 --> 00:01:05.619
We haven’t seen the full extent of his strength,
but he has the powers of a Special Grade sorcerer

00:01:05.619 --> 00:01:07.830
and then some.

00:01:07.830 --> 00:01:14.270
Only characters like Gojo Satoru make him
hesitate, but he’ll gladly take on other

00:01:14.270 --> 00:01:17.810
fighters without fear.

00:01:17.810 --> 00:01:29.560
What makes this mysterious figure so willing
to go head to head with other powerful characters?

00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:38.710
Kenjaku has a complete mastery of Cursed Energy,
being able to utilize massive quantities of

00:01:38.710 --> 00:01:40.920
it with ease.

00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:46.020
This allows him to be an excellent hand-to-hand
fighter by enhancing his physical attributes

00:01:46.020 --> 00:01:47.210
with cursed energy.

00:01:47.210 --> 00:01:52.140
After all, he has literally hundreds of years
of experience using this power.

00:01:52.140 --> 00:01:58.380
In addition, he’s also mastered other applications
of cursed energy such as barrier techniques

00:01:58.380 --> 00:02:03.600
and can even use a Domain Expansion without
setting up a barrier, a feat we’ve only

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:06.380
seen matched by Sukuna.

00:02:06.380 --> 00:02:13.510
In his fight against Yuki, he activates a
domain expansion called Womb Profusion, but

00:02:13.510 --> 00:02:18.650
other than the disturbing name, we don’t
know what it specifically does other than

00:02:18.650 --> 00:02:20.870
pack a crazy punch.

00:02:20.870 --> 00:02:28.090
However, Kenjaku’s true power comes from
the innate technique unique only to him: Kenjaku’s

00:02:28.090 --> 00:02:32.069
innate cursed technique is his ability to
switch bodies, which means he’s assumed

00:02:32.069 --> 00:02:36.489
tons of different identities over the course
of Jujutsu history.

00:02:36.489 --> 00:02:41.310
Only a few of those identities are known,
but it’s assumed he’s secretly been many

00:02:41.310 --> 00:02:42.790
people over time.

00:02:42.790 --> 00:02:46.709
And I use the word “secretly” lightly,
because it’s pretty obvious that someone

00:02:46.709 --> 00:02:52.879
is actually Kenjaku due to the massive surgical
scar on their forehead.

00:02:52.879 --> 00:03:00.430
He doesn’t just take over people’s bodies,
though: Kenjaku can also steal someone else’s

00:03:00.430 --> 00:03:05.790
cursed technique, giving him quite the collection
of deadly abilities.

00:03:05.790 --> 00:03:12.760
He’s been working on this master plan of
his for centuries, using each of his different

00:03:12.760 --> 00:03:15.760
identities to work toward this ultimate goal.

00:03:15.760 --> 00:03:21.150
So who has he been and why has he chosen to
take over these specific bodies?

00:03:21.150 --> 00:03:25.400
Let’s take a look at each and every one
of Kenjaku’s abilities

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:30.340
The earliest known identity is…well, Kenjaku
himself.

00:03:30.340 --> 00:03:35.769
Obviously there had to be a first Kenjaku
before he started inhabiting other people’s

00:03:35.769 --> 00:03:36.769
bodies.

00:03:36.769 --> 00:03:42.060
It’s unclear whether certain feats were
done as this original Kenjaku or later on

00:03:42.060 --> 00:03:44.090
down the line under an unknown identity.

00:03:44.090 --> 00:03:51.489
However, we know that even in the ancient
era, he was supremely powerful.

00:03:51.489 --> 00:03:55.180
He was once friends with the similarly old
Tengen.

00:03:55.180 --> 00:04:00.510
And he’s even the one who figured out how
to turn a sorcerer into a Cursed Object after

00:04:00.510 --> 00:04:05.620
their death, allowing Sukuna to be turned
into the 20 fingers that Yuji would one day

00:04:05.620 --> 00:04:06.730
eat.

00:04:06.730 --> 00:04:11.870
The most renowned of Kenjaku’s identities
was that of Noritoshi Kamo, the so-called

00:04:11.870 --> 00:04:14.420
most evil sorcerer in history.

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:20.539
Not to be confused with his descendant Noritoshi
Kamo the Kyoto Jujutsu High student.

00:04:20.539 --> 00:04:26.230
As a Kamo, the OG Noritoshi was part of the
Big Three Jujutsu Families, though he’s

00:04:26.230 --> 00:04:29.460
now considered a stain on their family.

00:04:29.460 --> 00:04:34.320
His claim to evil fame was his creation of
the Cursed Womb: Death Paintings.

00:04:34.320 --> 00:04:40.790
These were Kenjaku’s first attempt at creating
beings beyond humanity or cursed spirits.

00:04:40.790 --> 00:04:45.900
He kidnapped and held a woman prisoner who
was capable of giving birth to human-spirit

00:04:45.900 --> 00:04:46.900
hybrids.

00:04:46.900 --> 00:04:51.910
His wicked experiments with this ability lead
to the nine Death Paintings - though, I’ve

00:04:51.910 --> 00:04:58.270
gotta say - despite his messed up origins,
Choso turned out to be a pretty nice guy!

00:04:58.270 --> 00:05:04.810
It’s through his Kamo ancestry that Choso
was able to use the family’s special technique,

00:05:04.810 --> 00:05:06.090
Blood Manipulation.

00:05:06.090 --> 00:05:11.169
It’s possible that Kenjaku can also use
this technique, since he gains the ability

00:05:11.169 --> 00:05:17.040
to use the innate techniques of the bodies
he inhabits, resulting in him collecting many

00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:21.830
powers, most of which we’ve yet to see him
use.

00:05:21.830 --> 00:05:27.160
The next Kenjaku identity we know of, jumping
ahead several hundred years, is Kaori Itadori.

00:05:27.160 --> 00:05:32.730
That’s right: Kenjaku is none other than
YUJI’s MOM.

00:05:32.730 --> 00:05:38.919
Like…this isn’t even a meme or a bit…The
main villain of the series is canonically

00:05:38.919 --> 00:05:41.449
the main character’s mom.

00:05:41.449 --> 00:05:48.200
And due to Kenjaku’s manipulative nature,
it seems like he probably had a hand in…creating…Yuji

00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:54.919
and probably has a hidden motive for doing
so, since he’s the main character and therefore

00:05:54.919 --> 00:05:57.340
he’s probably extra special.

00:05:57.340 --> 00:06:03.990
Also, due to this, the Death Paintings technically
actually are Yuji’s siblings in a way, so

00:06:03.990 --> 00:06:09.280
when Choso recognizes Yuji as his brother…well,
he’s not wrong.

00:06:09.280 --> 00:06:12.060
We don’t know much about Kaori.

00:06:12.060 --> 00:06:15.870
Other than the reveal that she was possessed
by Kenjaku and had the signature forehead

00:06:15.870 --> 00:06:18.949
scar, we really haven’t learned all that
much.

00:06:18.949 --> 00:06:24.080
However, we do know her innate cursed technique…but
more on that later.

00:06:24.080 --> 00:06:30.210
The last known vessel for Kenjaku, and his
current one, is the one we know the most about:

00:06:30.210 --> 00:06:37.770
Special Grade Sorcerer Suguru Geto - former
bestie of Gojo Satoru and known human hater.

00:06:37.770 --> 00:06:42.560
After Geto’s death at the hands of his bestie
Gojo, his body became the current vessel for

00:06:42.560 --> 00:06:43.580
Kenjaku.

00:06:43.580 --> 00:06:48.550
This allowed him access to Geto’s innate
technique of Cursed Spirit Manipulation - an

00:06:48.550 --> 00:06:54.229
ability that would be instrumental in activating
his master plans.

00:06:54.229 --> 00:07:01.490
After assuming Suguru Geto’s identity, Kenjaku
allied with the Disaster Curses.

00:07:01.490 --> 00:07:06.960
This team consisting of Mahito, the Human
Curse; Jogo, the Volcano Curse; Hanami, the

00:07:06.960 --> 00:07:09.930
Nature Curse; and Dagon, the Ocean Curse.

00:07:09.930 --> 00:07:14.889
This group of Special Grade curses has the
goal of completely wiping out humanity so

00:07:14.889 --> 00:07:19.979
that curses can become the dominant species
on Earth.

00:07:19.979 --> 00:07:25.260
They meet with Kenjaku, who is posing as Geto,
who allies with them in order to help them

00:07:25.260 --> 00:07:28.550
get rid of Gojo Satoru using the Prison Realm.

00:07:28.550 --> 00:07:32.470
On the surface, they have plenty in common.

00:07:32.470 --> 00:07:38.440
Both Geto and the Disaster Curses hate humans,
since Geto sees them as below sorcerers.

00:07:38.440 --> 00:07:42.890
Geto goes as far as calling normal humans
who can’t manipulate cursed energy “monkeys”

00:07:42.890 --> 00:07:47.050
and believes they are completely inferior.

00:07:47.050 --> 00:07:52.340
He also has all the reason to want revenge
against Gojo for defeating him in the past.

00:07:52.340 --> 00:07:57.470
However, in reality, Kenjaku actually has
an ulterior motive.

00:07:57.470 --> 00:08:03.009
It’s true that he wants to get Gojo out
of the way - just like he’s the biggest

00:08:03.009 --> 00:08:08.580
obstacle for the Disaster Curses, he’s also
the biggest obstacle for Kenjaku.

00:08:08.580 --> 00:08:13.729
Because Kenjaku has a plan that’s been a
thousand years in the making and he can’t

00:08:13.729 --> 00:08:15.840
let Gojo go ruining it.

00:08:15.840 --> 00:08:21.270
There’s another reason for him to ally with
these curses - and it comes right down to

00:08:21.270 --> 00:08:28.070
how he’s a master manipulator who’s just
using them for his own goals all along.

00:08:28.070 --> 00:08:32.080
Instead of doing all of the work himself,
Kenjaku allows these Disaster Curses to use

00:08:32.080 --> 00:08:39.190
their immense strength to start enacting his
plans for him.

00:08:39.190 --> 00:08:41.130
Everything Kenjaku does is manipulative.

00:08:41.130 --> 00:08:46.830
I mean, what’s more manipulative than literally
taking over someone’s body?

00:08:46.830 --> 00:08:51.640
Kenjaku delights in making people bend to
his whims all the while thinking that they’re

00:08:51.640 --> 00:08:54.380
working in their own self-interest.

00:08:54.380 --> 00:08:59.960
No matter the situation, Kenjaku is always
in complete control and uses his tactical

00:08:59.960 --> 00:09:03.880
genius to stay several steps ahead of his
enemies.

00:09:03.880 --> 00:09:08.700
He even hides the true extent of most of his
powers so that he can have the upper hand

00:09:08.700 --> 00:09:10.170
in combat.

00:09:10.170 --> 00:09:14.230
But why is he doing any of this in the first
place?

00:09:14.230 --> 00:09:19.260
What is Kenjaku’s real end goal that took
a millennium of preparation?

00:09:19.260 --> 00:09:23.700
Well, to tell you I’m going to have to get
into some manga spoilers so while everything

00:09:23.700 --> 00:09:28.500
so far is covered in the Shibuya Incident
in season 2 of the anime, from here on out,

00:09:28.500 --> 00:09:33.130
we’re looking at what we know about Kenjaku
from the manga so far.

00:09:33.130 --> 00:09:40.760
Well, Kenjaku’s motive in the story is to
test the limits of cursed energy and push

00:09:40.760 --> 00:09:45.880
beyond all conventions and boundaries of the
powers within JJK.

00:09:45.880 --> 00:09:50.890
He believes that human beings who wield cursed
energy and cursed spirits can’t be the end

00:09:50.890 --> 00:09:52.850
all be all of Jujutsu.

00:09:52.850 --> 00:09:58.550
He believes that something greater than either
of these entities must be possible.

00:09:58.550 --> 00:10:05.540
In fact, this is why he made the Cursed Womb:
Death Paintings back when he assumed the identity

00:10:05.540 --> 00:10:07.230
of Noritoshi Kamo.

00:10:07.230 --> 00:10:12.450
Ultimately, Kenjaku determined that the Death
Paintings were failures because his “children”

00:10:12.450 --> 00:10:14.980
could not surpass him.

00:10:14.980 --> 00:10:20.730
He came to believe that nothing he personally
created could ever surpass himself, so he

00:10:20.730 --> 00:10:27.630
made it his goal to use uncontrollable, unpredictable
chaos to advance his goals.

00:10:27.630 --> 00:10:29.720
Enter the Culling Game: The way he plans to
create these higher beings is through his

00:10:29.720 --> 00:10:35.010
twisted Culling Game, a lethal battle royale
that pits Japan’s strongest Jujutsu Sorcerers

00:10:35.010 --> 00:10:36.450
against one another.

00:10:36.450 --> 00:10:46.339
This allows Gege Akutami to write his take
on a Manga Classic: The Tournament Arc, because

00:10:46.339 --> 00:10:50.149
who doesn’t love a good battle Shonen staple.

00:10:50.149 --> 00:10:57.810
However, this tournament is actually a ritual
which draws out a huge amount of cursed energy.

00:10:57.810 --> 00:11:06.070
Another one of his identities, which is thus
far unknown, made binding vows with several

00:11:06.070 --> 00:11:10.070
powerful sorcerers from the past, so that
they could one day compete in the Culling

00:11:10.070 --> 00:11:11.070
Game.

00:11:11.070 --> 00:11:18.130
By promising them a second chance at life,
he convinced these sorcerers to be turned

00:11:18.130 --> 00:11:24.839
into cursed objects that could be resurrected
later on.These include great fighters like

00:11:24.839 --> 00:11:29.180
Hajime Kashimo who can even throw down with
the likes of Sukuna.

00:11:29.180 --> 00:11:33.050
This shows just how long Kenjaku’s been
working on his master plan.

00:11:33.050 --> 00:11:37.700
In the present day, he was able to activate
the spirits of these sorcerers to take over

00:11:37.700 --> 00:11:43.360
human vessels he had prepared so that these
warriors of the past could participate in

00:11:43.360 --> 00:11:44.820
the game.

00:11:44.820 --> 00:11:51.260
This happens in a very similar way to how
Yuji became a vessel for Sukuna, with humans

00:11:51.260 --> 00:11:56.690
ingesting cursed objects that contained the
sorcerer’s cursed energy.

00:11:56.690 --> 00:12:01.459
Other people still were newly awakened as
sorcerers who hadn’t formerly had access

00:12:01.459 --> 00:12:03.630
to cursed energy.

00:12:03.630 --> 00:12:11.760
How the actual ritual works is a bit complicated
and we don’t have every single detail yet.

00:12:11.760 --> 00:12:19.490
Kenjaku’s true aim is to use this concentration
of cursed energy to fuse every non-sorcerer

00:12:19.490 --> 00:12:23.579
human in Japan with Master Tengen.

00:12:23.579 --> 00:12:28.290
Tengen is the ancient sorcerer who lives in
the Tombs of the Star Corridor, generating

00:12:28.290 --> 00:12:33.510
the barriers that protect the Jujutsu High
campuses.Tengen’s abilities have already

00:12:33.510 --> 00:12:37.449
transcended humanity, making him immortal.

00:12:37.449 --> 00:12:43.300
In fact, he’s lived so long that he knew
Kenjaku 1,000 years ago when both were young.

00:12:43.300 --> 00:12:47.690
They were even friends at one point, but clearly
there’s been quite a lot of division between

00:12:47.690 --> 00:12:51.120
them over the past millennium.

00:12:51.120 --> 00:12:59.380
Since his Star Vessel was killed and he wasn’t
able to merge with her, Tengen’s evolving

00:12:59.380 --> 00:13:01.800
at an alarming rate.

00:13:01.800 --> 00:13:07.170
By merging with the star vessel, he’s usually
able to pause his alarming rate of evolution..

00:13:07.170 --> 00:13:10.750
Now, his appearance doesn’t even appear
human anymore.

00:13:10.750 --> 00:13:15.889
Kenjaku plans on using the fact that Tengen
has already become something beyond human

00:13:15.889 --> 00:13:19.010
to his advantage.

00:13:19.010 --> 00:13:25.230
The true reason Kenjaku used the Disaster
Curses is because he needs their power - specifically

00:13:25.230 --> 00:13:26.720
the power of Mahito.

00:13:26.720 --> 00:13:33.240
By using Suguru’s ultimate technique, Maximum:
Uzumaki, he is able to absorb the innate techniques

00:13:33.240 --> 00:13:35.490
of powerful Cursed Spirits.

00:13:35.490 --> 00:13:40.209
He needed Mahito’s power of Idle Transfiguration
because that’s the key to taking down the

00:13:40.209 --> 00:13:46.380
powerful barrier around Tengen, which is no
easy feat since Tengen is the most powerful

00:13:46.380 --> 00:13:49.730
barrier user in history.

00:13:49.730 --> 00:13:54.399
This is yet another way that Kenjaku is a
master manipulator.

00:13:54.399 --> 00:14:00.490
He got four Special Grade curses who hated
humanity to essentially complete his plans

00:14:00.490 --> 00:14:01.490
for him.

00:14:01.490 --> 00:14:04.509
Kenjaku is always using others for his own
purposes.

00:14:04.509 --> 00:14:09.620
He used the Disaster Curses to help him seal
Gojo, and he promised the ancient sorcerers

00:14:09.620 --> 00:14:15.060
to be turned into Cursed Objects just so he
could use them as sacrificial pawns in his

00:14:15.060 --> 00:14:16.060
Culling Game.

00:14:16.060 --> 00:14:20.420
When he needs more bloodshed to occur in the
Culling Game to draw out even more cursed

00:14:20.420 --> 00:14:27.589
energy, he even manipulates the entire U.S.
Government by convincing the President about

00:14:27.589 --> 00:14:32.500
Cursed Energy’s potential military uses,
causing tons of soldiers to be slaughtered

00:14:32.500 --> 00:14:36.899
as they entered the combat zones without any
mastery of cursed energy.

00:14:36.899 --> 00:14:42.610
Back to the master plan, though: By dissolving
his protective barrier, and completing the

00:14:42.610 --> 00:14:47.390
Culling Game, Kenjaku plans to force humanity
to evolve into a state beyond its current

00:14:47.390 --> 00:14:52.860
existence by forcefully fusing all of Japan’s
non sorcerers with Tengen.

00:14:52.860 --> 00:14:58.779
And unfortunately for Japan, Kenjaku has already
managed to dissolve the protective barrier.This

00:14:58.779 --> 00:15:03.980
was despite Tengen being guarded by the Special
Grade Sorcer, Yuki - you know, the lady who

00:15:03.980 --> 00:15:08.980
makes a habit of asking much younger boys
what type of girls they like - for a minute,

00:15:08.980 --> 00:15:12.000
it looked like Kenjaku he was on the ropes.

00:15:12.000 --> 00:15:17.360
The combined efforts of Yuki and Choso (who
again, is technically kind of Kenjaku’s

00:15:17.360 --> 00:15:20.839
son) gave him a real challenge.

00:15:20.839 --> 00:15:26.079
Yuki’s Cursed Technique manipulates gravity,
which seemed like it would quite literally

00:15:26.079 --> 00:15:31.399
crush anything Kenjaku could throw at her…However,
he was able to conjure up the cursed technique

00:15:31.399 --> 00:15:34.920
of one of his previous bodies to counter Yuki’s
ability.

00:15:34.920 --> 00:15:40.639
And this was the technique of none other than
Yuji’s Mom!

00:15:40.639 --> 00:15:45.339
Kaori Itadori’s cursed technique is called
the Anti-Gravity System, which was a huge

00:15:45.339 --> 00:15:49.980
stroke of luck when Kenjaku had to battle
Yuki and her gravity based powers.

00:15:49.980 --> 00:15:55.579
It’s quite literally the perfect counter,
so who knows how many other secret techniques

00:15:55.579 --> 00:16:00.540
from his previous bodies Kenjaku has lying
around, ready to use at the perfect moment

00:16:00.540 --> 00:16:03.880
to catch his opponents off guard.

00:16:03.880 --> 00:16:08.449
Having such a huge assortment of techniques
to choose from is one thing that helps Kenjaku

00:16:08.449 --> 00:16:16.330
stay one step ahead of everyone as he enacts
his plan.

00:16:16.330 --> 00:16:23.519
Even Kenjaku has no idea what the result of
the Culling Game ritual will be - he’s just

00:16:23.519 --> 00:16:26.449
sickeningly curious to see what happens.

00:16:26.449 --> 00:16:31.589
He even believes that if the resulting being
just takes the shape of a silly face, it’ll

00:16:31.589 --> 00:16:37.149
just be comical to him, even as he essentially
dooms humanity as we know it.

00:16:37.149 --> 00:16:41.280
After all, Kenjaku definitely has a sense
of humor.

00:16:41.280 --> 00:16:46.259
As opposed&nbsp; to a lot of anime antagonists
who are deadly serious and calm, cool, and

00:16:46.259 --> 00:16:50.149
collected at all times - Kenjaku is pretty
silly.

00:16:50.149 --> 00:16:54.330
This is best displayed in his battle with
Fumihiko Takaba.

00:16:54.330 --> 00:16:58.620
Fumihiko is one of the ordinary people who
suddenly found himself with cursed powers

00:16:58.620 --> 00:17:00.810
at the start of the Culling Game.

00:17:00.810 --> 00:17:04.400
Fumihiko Takaba is a comedian - albeit a failed
one.

00:17:04.400 --> 00:17:08.709
However, his cursed technique is entirely
based on his comedy style and involves turning

00:17:08.709 --> 00:17:14.199
his imagination into reality - an ability
that will become ridiculously powerful if

00:17:14.199 --> 00:17:15.620
he can master it.

00:17:15.620 --> 00:17:20.850
As he tries to take down the mastermind Kenjaku,
it becomes just as much a battle of wits as

00:17:20.850 --> 00:17:22.470
it is a battle of strength.

00:17:22.470 --> 00:17:26.640
However, much to Takaba’s surprise, as they
test each other to see who can make the other

00:17:26.640 --> 00:17:31.570
laugh…Kenjaku might actually be funnier
than the professional comedian.

00:17:31.570 --> 00:17:36.650
He’s a master of creating goofy faces, and
even knows a lot about various popular comedy

00:17:36.650 --> 00:17:38.760
TV programs in Japan.

00:17:38.760 --> 00:17:43.309
Much like Gojo, he apparently had a lot of
time to watch his share of movies in between

00:17:43.309 --> 00:17:45.890
creating his evil schemes.

00:17:45.890 --> 00:17:51.130
Kenjaku has actually adapted surprisingly
well to the modern era considering he’s

00:17:51.130 --> 00:17:53.000
1,000 years old.

00:17:53.000 --> 00:17:57.620
You’d expect him to be behind the times,
but in addition to keeping up with television,

00:17:57.620 --> 00:18:00.980
he can also be seen playing the Game of Life
with the Disaster Curses.

00:18:00.980 --> 00:18:06.380
This is nothing compared to the time Kenjaku
pulls out a whole iPhone so he can read chapter

00:18:06.380 --> 00:18:08.450
236 of Jujutsu Kaisen…

00:18:08.450 --> 00:18:13.440
Okay, so it’s implied that he actually just
has some kind of surveillance operating so

00:18:13.440 --> 00:18:17.990
he can check out the Gojo vs. Sukuna fight
from afar, but since the literal manga panel

00:18:17.990 --> 00:18:22.400
of Gojo’s death is superimposed over his
phone screen, it definitely just looks like

00:18:22.400 --> 00:18:25.010
Kenjaku downloaded the Shonen Jump app.

00:18:25.010 --> 00:18:30.250
Either way, the man has definitely adapted
to the 21st century and all of the technological

00:18:30.250 --> 00:18:31.940
marvels that come with it.

00:18:31.940 --> 00:18:37.350
Pretty impressive for somebody who lived all
the way back in the Heian era of Japan.

00:18:37.350 --> 00:18:43.090
It’s just another way that this villain
continues to shock the audience and defy expectations.

00:18:43.090 --> 00:18:49.970
His culling game plan is for little other
than his own twisted amusement and entertainment.

00:18:49.970 --> 00:18:55.870
Out of sheer curiosity, Kenjaku is perfectly
willing to sacrifice the entire population

00:18:55.870 --> 00:18:58.539
of Japan just so he can see what happens.

00:18:58.539 --> 00:19:04.120
He is at one time cold and calculating while
also being fun-loving in the most deranged

00:19:04.120 --> 00:19:06.110
and chaotic way.

00:19:06.110 --> 00:19:11.910
This allowed him to set his Culling Game plan
in action and lead to the most intense JJK

00:19:11.910 --> 00:19:17.580
arc yet, where we’re going to find out even
more about this evil mastermind and more importantly

00:19:17.580 --> 00:19:19.360
have some epic battles.

00:19:19.360 --> 00:19:25.140
And perhaps the biggest mystery still is what
role Yuji Itadori has to play in all of this.

00:19:25.140 --> 00:19:29.820
Surely Yuji being able to act as a vessel
for Sukuna and being literally birthed by

00:19:29.820 --> 00:19:36.000
the main villain of the story have some connection,
but what part he plays in Kenjaku’s plan

00:19:36.000 --> 00:19:38.810
is still a completely mystery.

00:19:38.810 --> 00:19:43.900
With all of Kenjaku’s crazy powers, watching
even a single fight of his can get hard to

00:19:43.900 --> 00:19:48.630
wrap your mind around since he’s busting
out cursed techniques left and right.

00:19:48.630 --> 00:19:52.500
Between cursed technique, and reversed cursed
techniques, and innate techniques, there are

00:19:52.500 --> 00:19:54.630
just so many techniques to understand!

00:19:54.630 --> 00:20:00.810
Thankfully understanding all of these is easy:
all you have to do is watch this video that

00:20:00.810 --> 00:20:04.130
explains the whole JJK Power System

